# Call-site ledger of segno at 9b67a3f2914be966c35dd8f00bef19d01b9ec68e.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in segno.md.
#
# Facts used throughout (segno.md, "Architecture"):
# - A QRCode has __slots__; QRCode.__init__ sets every slot, and the package
#   loads on a QRCode only these slots, its properties and its methods. No
#   property raises AttributeError, so QRCode.__getattr__ runs only for a
#   name that the class lacks: the client's to_<name> plugin names and the
#   names that QRCodeSequence.__getattr__ forwards (1016:27).
# - A QRCodeSequence is a tuple of QRCode objects; the package loads only
#   terminal and save on it, which the class defines.
# - Buffer and Segments (encoder.py) are private; the package subscripts,
#   measures and iterates them only at the sites that accept their methods.
# - The writers get `out` from QRCode.save: a file name, the package's own
#   io.BytesIO (svg_inline, as_svg_data_uri, as_png_data_uri), the tempfile
#   wrapper of QRCode.show (a .png), the gzip.GzipFile of an .svgz file
#   name, or a client stream (opaque, B5: the stub annotation
#   out: IO[AnyStr] | str fixes no stream class; the referee's ruling).
default reject segno.QRCode.__getattr__, segno.QRCodeSequence.__getattr__: no attribute load at this site misses on a QRCode or a QRCodeSequence: the receiver is a module, a str, bytes, a builtin container, an io or codecs stream, an argparse object, a Segments, Buffer, _Segment, _StructuredAppendInfo or EC object, a function, or a QRCode/QRCodeSequence whose attribute (a slot set in __init__, a property, a method, or __class__) exists, so normal lookup succeeds and no __getattr__ runs
default reject segno.encoder.Buffer.__getitem__, segno.encoder.Segments.__getitem__: the subscripted object (or the iterable that a builtin indexes) is not a Buffer or a Segments: it is a tuple, list, bytearray, bytes, str, dict, range or namedtuple of the package or of the client; only the sites that accept them subscript a Buffer (add_codewords) or a Segments (QRCode.__init__)
default reject segno.encoder.Buffer.__len__, segno.encoder.Segments.__len__: the measured or truth-tested object is not a Buffer or a Segments: it is a str, bytes, bytearray, tuple, list, dict, set or a client value; only the sites that accept them measure a Buffer or a Segments
default reject segno.encoder.Segments.__iter__: the iterated object is not a Segments: it is a tuple, list, bytearray, bytes, str, dict view, range, generator or an itertools object; only the for loop of _encode (225:20) iterates a Segments
default reject segno.QRCode.__eq__: no operand of this comparison, `in` test or dict/set key lookup is a QRCode: the package compares ints, strs, bytes, bytearrays, tuples, lists, colors and None, and QRCode is unhashable (__hash__ = None), so it is never a dict key or set element; QRCode.__eq__ itself compares classes and matrices (tuples of bytearrays)
